  "body_text": "Passports | Adams County, Idaho WebFont.load({  google: {    families: [\"Lato:100,100italic,300,300italic,400,400italic,700,700italic,900,900italic\",\"Exo:100,100italic,200,200italic,300,300italic,400,400italic,500,500italic,600,600italic,700,700italic,800,800italic,900,900italic\"]  }}); !function(o,c){var n=c.documentElement,t=\" w-mod-\";n.className+=t+\"js\",(\"ontouchstart\"in o||o.DocumentTouch&&c instanceof DocumentTouch)&&(n.className+=t+\"touch\")}(window,document); (function(w,i,g){w[g]=w[g]||[];if(typeof w[g].push=='function')w[g].push.apply(w[g],Array.isArray(i)?i:[i]);})(window,['G-7PT243DPQG','UA-182726589-2'],'google_tags_first_party'); window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}gtag('set', 'developer_id.dZGVlNj', true);gtag('set', 'developer_id.dYWYxNW', true);gtag('js', new Date());gtag('config', 'G-7PT243DPQG');gtag('config', 'UA-182726589-2', {'anonymize_ip': true}); Adams County, Idaho Adams County’s core purpose is to provide quality public services, ensure public safety, and promote the preservation and management of natural resources for the well-being of our citizens ‍ I want to . . . Appeal Assessed Value Apply for a job Find Election Information Find Court Assistance Get a Passport Pay Property tax Read County Ordinances Register a Vehicle Request Records from Sheriff Renew Driver's License Search Recorded Documents Departments Assessor Building Department Clerk | Auditor | Recorder Commissioners Coroner Judicial Planning & Zoning Prosecutor Road & Bridge Sheriff Treasurer Waste Management & Recycling Weed Control Quick Links Adams County Ordinances Citizen's Report Council Valley Ambulance District Court Self Help Driver's License Emergency Management Inciweb Fire Map Marriage Licenses Parks & Recreation Pay Court Fees Probation Public Meetings Public Notices Recorded Documents Register to Vote Soil & Water Conservation District Vehicle Registration GIS Maps Home Adams County, Idaho Adams County’s core purpose is to provide quality public services, ensure public safety, and promote the preservation and management of natural resources for the well-being of our citizens. I Want To . . . Appeal Assessed Value Apply for a Job Find Election Information Find Court Assistance File a Citizen's Report Get a Passport Pay Property Tax Read County Ordinances Register a Vehicle Renew Driver's License Request Records from Sheriff Search Recorded Documents Departments Assessor Building Department Clerk | Auditor | Recorder Commissioners Coroner Judicial Office Planning & Zoning Prosecuting Attorney Road & Bridge Sheriff Treasurer Waste Management |  Recycling Weed Control Quick Links Adams County Ordinances Citizen's Report Council Valley Ambulance District Court Records Request Court Self Help Driver's License Emergency Management InciWeb Fire Map Marriage Licenses Parks & Recreation Pay Court Fees Probation Public Meetings Public Notices Recorded Documents Register to Vote Soil & Water Conservation District Vehicle Registration GIS Maps Clerk Home Email thorton@co.adams.id.us Hours 8AM- 5PM Monday - Friday Phone  (208) 253-4561 Option 5 Fax (208) 253-4880 Mailing Address PO Box 48 Council, ID 83612 Physical Address 201 Industrial Ave. Council, ID 83612 Passports Applications for passports are available from the County Clerk’s Office in the Courthouse. We will accept passports M-Th 8:00am-4:30pm and Fridays from 8:00am-4:00pm You can also go to  https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/passports/requirements/forms.html  and print out the needed passport application. This site also contains information on passport services and other passport-related information. To obtain a passport, you must come into the Clerk’s Office in person. You will need: Completed, but unsigned, passport application (DS-11). It must be signed in the presence of an authorized clerk in the Recorder’s office.   Two identical 2”x2” passport photos. These must have been taken in the last six months and have a light background. Birth certificate with a raised seal, issued by the state where applicant was born. Hospital certificates and birth abstracts are not acceptable.** If you are a naturalized citizen you must bring your original naturalization papers. All original documents that are sent with your application are returned to you with your passport. Current driver’s license or some other form of photo ID. FEES for routine passport applications may be paid using a money order, cashier’s check or personal check. Fees are non-refundable. PASSPORT BOOK For ages 16 and older: $130 Payable to Dept. of State, plus $35 Payable to Adams County For ages under 16: $100 Payable to Dept. of States, plus $35 Payable to Adams County PASSPORT CARD For ages 16 and older: $30 Payable to Dept. of State, plus $35 Payable to Adams County For ages under 16: $15 Payable to Dept. of State, plus $35 Payable to Adams County Passport Renewal (Form DS-82) If you can answer “yes” to all the following statements, you can use the DS-82. (Adams County does not do renewals, but carries the DS-82 forms). I can submit my most recent U.S. passport book and/or U.S. passport card with this application. I was at least 16 years old when my most recent U.S. passport book and/or U.S. Passport card was issued. I was issued my most recent U.S. passport book and/or U.S. Passport card less than 15 years ago. I use the same name as on my most recent U.S. passport book and/or U.S. Passport card -OR- I have had my name changed by marriage or court order and can submit proper documentation to reflect my name change. If you answered NO to any of the four statements above, you cannot use the DS-82. You must apply on application form DS-11 by making a personal appearance before an acceptance agent authorized to accept passport applications, such as the Clerk’s Office in Adams County. The non-refundable total fee for the renewal is $130. Expedited Service For any expedited service (e.g., first-time application, renewal, additional pages, name change) there is an additional service fee of $60. We  strongly suggest  that you use overnight delivery service to return your newly issued Passport Book to you. Overnight delivery service is not available for passport cards, which are delivered via First Class Mail only. The current Overnight Delivery Fee is $18.32. Clerk Pages Clerk Home Election Information Liquor Licenses Marriage Licenses Passports Recordable Documents Search Your Government Departments Assessor Building Department Clerk | Auditor | Recorder Commissioners Coroner Election Information Judicial Planning & Zoning Prosecuting Attorney Road & Bridge Sheriff Treasurer Waste Management | Recycling Weed Control Common Links Adams County Jobs Council Valley Ambulance District Court Forms Court Records Request Emergency Management Landfill Hours Online Voter Registration Pay Court Fees Pay Property Taxes Public Meetings Public Notices Search Recorded Documents Community Links Adams County Health Center Adams County Parks & Rec Adams County Rodeo Boise VA Medical Center Council Chamber of Commerce City of Council Council Library Council Schools City of New Meadows New Meadows Library New Meadows Schools Soil & Water Conservation District U of I Extension Address: 201 Industrial Ave. Council, Idaho 83612  |  County Offices (208) 253-4561  |  Sheriff (208) 253-4227  |  Website Policies  |  Sitemap  |  Editor  |  Employee Portal The information displayed or linked on this website may not reflect the most current, correct, or relevant legal or factual premises. Adams County provides this site for general informational purposes only and does not guarantee its accuracy or availability. The contents of this site should not be relied upon as advice of any kind or as a definitive authority in any matter; rather than so relying, you are encouraged to contact Adams County directly or seek assistance from a qualified professional to address any questions relevant to 